# 1Password value resolution for directorate-of-equality-web — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# See config/1password/README.md for the model, the caching note, how to migrate
# an app, and why decorator names must not appear in prose in this file.

# @defaultRequired=infer
# @plugin(@varlock/1password-plugin)
# @initOp(token=$OP_TOKEN, allowAppAuth=true)
# @setValuesBulk(opLoadEnvironment($OP_SHARED_ENVIRONMENT))
# @setValuesBulk(opLoadEnvironment($OP_APP_ENVIRONMENT))
# @import(../../../apps/directorate-of-equality-web/)
# ---

# Empty, so this falls back to desktop-app authentication.
#
# DISABLED, NOT ABANDONED -- to re-enable, delete the empty assignment below and
# uncomment the keychain line under it. Nothing else needs to change.
#
# The intent is a scoped, read-only 1Password service account whose token lives
# in the macOS Keychain rather than in a file or the shell. Desktop-app auth
# authorises PER RUN, so every `nx serve` prompts; it also connects as the
# developer with their full vault access, where a service account can be limited
# to just the dev environments. keychain() still authenticates, but per SESSION.
#
# It is off because the service account could not read the shared environment:
# resolution failed at the first setValuesBulk line with "an unexpected error
# occurred while processing the request". The token itself resolved from the
# Keychain fine. Turn this back on once the service account has read access to
# the shared environment plus every app environment it needs.
#
# The Keychain account name is pinned rather than defaulted. varlock derives the
# default from the current directory name, so it differs between the main
# checkout and each worktree, and a ref written in one would not resolve in the
# other. Create the item with:
#
#   varlock keychain set        OP_TOKEN --account dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN
#   varlock keychain fix-access          --account dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN
#
# allowAppAuth stays true above, so anyone without the Keychain item keeps
# working through the desktop app rather than failing outright.
# @type=opServiceAccountToken @internal
OP_TOKEN=
# OP_TOKEN=keychain("varlock", account="dmr.is:local:OP_TOKEN")

# Holds only keys that are either byte-identical across every deployed service
# (IDENTITY_SERVER_DOMAIN, the four NATIONAL_REGISTRY_*, XROAD_DMR_CLIENT,
# XROAD_ISLAND_IS_PATH) or absent from every deployment and the same on every
# laptop (LOCAL_CHROMIUM_PATH). Nothing else. Keep it disjoint from the app environment
# below -- which of the two wins for a duplicated key is still unverified, so a
# key must live in exactly one of them.
# @public @internal
OP_SHARED_ENVIRONMENT=xg6t32oousqpfj5lbmj4gpjxqe

# Everything this app needs, named as its ECS task definition names it.
# @public @internal
OP_APP_ENVIRONMENT=knwr2j7slcgxbgq43ypijewgcu
